# {{ business.name }}

A static website built with [Astro](https://astro.build) and Tailwind CSS,
generated by `sitegen`.

## Running it

```bash
npm install
npm run dev      # http://localhost:4321
npm run build    # static output in dist/
npm run preview  # serve the built output
```

## Editing the content

Every piece of text on the page comes from `src/data/business.json`. Edit a
value there and the page follows — you do not need to touch the components.

Sections disappear on their own when their data is empty, so deleting the
`services` array removes the services section from the page.

## Changing the colors and font

`src/styles/global.css` holds a `@theme` block with the full `brand-*` and
`accent-*` scales plus `--font-sans`. Those names become Tailwind utilities,
so `--color-brand-600` is usable as `bg-brand-600` or `text-brand-600`.

## Deploying

`npm run build` writes a plain static site to `dist/`, which any static host
will serve — Netlify, Vercel, Cloudflare Pages, GitHub Pages, or your own
server. Update `site` in `astro.config.mjs` to the real domain first, since
that value feeds the structured data used for search engine rich results.
